course: dictionary
lesson: 3770
title: A tiny pocket for every hair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every hair grows from a follicle, which is a tiny pocket or hole in the skin. Science words often explain themselves in the words around them. «Each hair grows from a follicle in the skin» tells you a follicle is part of the skin, and the hair starts there.
explain: «Follically challenged» is a joking way to say bald. The clue is in the next part of the sentence: follicles are the tiny holes hairs grow from. If there are no hairs growing, the joke makes sense.
explain: The strand of hair you can see is not the living part. «Only the root down in the follicle is alive, and the strand you see is dead keratin.» So the follicle is where the living root sits, deep in the skin.
explain: Look for the link between the follicle and the hair. «A round one grows straight hair, a flat or oval one grows curly hair.» The shape of the follicle decides the shape of the hair, just as the shape of a nozzle shapes the icing.
fact: A follicle is a tiny hole or pocket in the skin.
fact: Each hair grows from its own follicle, about 1 centimetre a month.
fact: «Follicle» can also mean a small sac inside the body, such as an egg in the ovary.
fact: The shape of the follicle decides whether a hair grows straight or curly.
fact: Cutting hair does not make it grow back thicker or faster, because the follicle is under the skin.
exercise: «Each hair grows from a follicle in the skin.» What is a follicle? | The part of the hair you can see above the skin | A type of shampoo | *A tiny hole or pocket in the skin where a hair grows
exercise: «The shape of the follicle decides the shape of the hair.» Which follicle shape grows curly hair? | Dry and empty | *Flat or oval | Round | Long and hanging out of the skin
exercise: «Follically challenged» is a joking way to say what? | *Bald | Very curly | Hungry | Full of shampoo
test: «Hair grows about one centimetre a month.» How much does hair grow in one month? | About 10 centimetres | *About 1 centimetre | About 10 metres | About 1 metre
test: «A new one grows from the same follicle.» Where does a new hair grow from after the old one falls out? | From the nail | Hair does not grow back | *From the same follicle | From a new hole in the skin
exam: «Only the root down in the follicle is alive, and the strand you see is dead keratin.» Which part of the hair is dead? | The root in the follicle | *The strand you can see above the skin | Both the root and the strand are alive | The follicle itself
